guide forever/horde/tauren/01-mulgore
title Mulgore
faction Horde
race Tauren
levels 1-12
zone Mulgore
next forever/horde/02-the-barrens

# Route: the simulator's consensus route for Tauren (data/sim/export/consensus-horde-tauren),
# visits 1-2: Mulgore 1-11.9 (bind Bloodhoof Village) and Thunder Bluff
# 11.9-12.1, ending at the Crossroads (flight path, bind).
#
# Flow: Camp Narache -> plainstriders and cougars -> Seer Graytongue -> the
# shrine of An'she and Mu'sha -> Brambleblade Ravine -> Camp Narache ->
# Bloodhoof Village (bind) -> Winterhoof Water Well -> Chakuyak and the
# northern plains -> Bloodhoof -> Thunderhorn Water Well -> Bloodhoof ->
# Winterhoof Water Well, the Rolling Plains, Galak centaurs and the Ravaged
# Caravan -> Bloodhoof -> Venture Co. Mine -> Wildmane Water Well and
# Windfury Ridge -> Bael'dun Digsite -> Palemane Rock -> Bloodhoof ->
# Winterhoof Water Well -> Red Rocks -> Thunder Bluff -> the Crossroads.
#
# Deviations from the export:
# - Break Sharptusk! (3376) is taken from Brave Windfeather at the second
#   Grull visit (it needs level 3), not at level 3.1 with the first hand-ins.
# - The Adventurer (96659) is taken from Chief Hawkwind when you leave Camp
#   Narache and handed to Kaga Wildhoof on the road into Bloodhoof; it unlocks
#   The Great Outdoors and Camping 101, which the export took earlier than
#   The Adventurer (impossible in game). All three are done on arrival.
# - A Task Unfinished (1656, Antur Fallow, handed to Innkeeper Kauth in
#   Bloodhoof) starts the cougar hunt instead of being a step of its own:
#   Antur stands at the camp's west end, by the cougars' north-west corner,
#   and the hunt goes on from him instead of walking back into the camp.
#   He lies off every walk out of the camp; taken after the hunt or on the
#   way to Seer Graytongue (about 230 yards out of the way) it is 0.002 h
#   later to 10 and 20 under the simulator, with the plainstriders 0.02 h,
#   so it stays first and saves the back-and-forth instead.
# - Fizsprocket's Notes (98424) and the Venture Co. quests (764, 765) share
#   one trip into the mine: the notes start from Supervisor Fizsprocket's drop,
#   so the export's first mine visit is folded into the second.
# - A Sacred Burial (833) and Rite of Wisdom (773) are done on one visit to
#   Red Rocks instead of two.
# - Durotar is no longer visited: the older guide went on from the Crossroads
#   to Razor Hill for Threat from Below (99048, 99049, 99051), Rezlak's
#   Stormy Potential (97281, 97282), Lost But Not Forgotten (816), Burning
#   Shadows (832) and Conscript of the Horde (840). Neither consensus route
#   goes there. Under the simulator this guide now reaches level 20 in
#   10.48 h, against 10.75 h for the previous version with the trip. The
#   Barrens guide starts at level 12.
# - Thunder Bluff stop after Red Rocks (added at the integrator's request;
#   class quests are not simulated): flight path, training, and the turn-ins
#   the export accepts but never hands in: Journey into Thunder Bluff (775),
#   The High Chieftain (99082), Thunderhorn's Report (98435), The Hunter's
#   Way (861) and The Longwalkers (98430, escorted out of Palemane Rock).
#   The export's hearth to Bloodhoof at 10.2 is not used; Druids hearth there
#   from Moonglade instead.
# - Added from the new consensus at the Thunder Bluff stop: Traditions of the
#   Bluff (97485, Forever: buy four incense parts from the city's vendors and
#   spread the incense on Hunter Rise; it shows the city's trades and rises),
#   and the breadcrumbs Sergra Darkthorn (860) and The Barrens Oases (886),
#   handed in on arrival at the Crossroads. Simulator cost of the three: 0.02
#   h to level 20, kept for the teaching quest.
#
# Class quests at 4: Shamans take Call of Earth (1519-1521) from Seer
# Ravenfeather when the ravine turn-ins in Camp Narache bring them to 4, then
# walk back to Brambleblade Ravine for the Bristleback Shamans' Ritual Salve;
# the Minor Manifestation of Earth waits on the mesa east of the camp.
#
# Class quests at 10 (Thunder Bluff stop):
# - Warrior: Veteran Uzzek (1505), continued in the Barrens guide.
# - Shaman: Call of Fire (1523), continued in the Barrens guide.
# - Hunter: The Hunter's Path (6065) and the taming chain at Bloodhoof (6061,
#   6087, 6088: Tame Beast) to Training the Beast (6089, Beast Training),
#   handed in on a flight back from the Crossroads.
# - Druid: Heeding the Call (5926) through the Great Bear Spirit in Moonglade
#   to Body and Heart (6002) at the Moonkin Stone in the eastern pass, handed
#   in on a flight back from the Crossroads.
#
# Class letters at 1: Grull Hawkwind's letter for each class (Simple Note
# 3091 Warrior, Etched Note 3092 Hunter, Rune-Inscribed Note 3093 Shaman,
# Verdant Note 3094 Druid) is taken after The Hunt Begins and handed to the
# trainer in Camp Narache.
#
# Class training: Camp Narache, Bloodhoof Village and Thunder Bluff.
#
# Data-less objectives: Grace of An'she and Mu'sha (95805) is a ten-minute
# run with the incense, handled as a direct turn-in at the shrine.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Camp Narache

step Camp Narache
  tip You start on the mesa of Camp Narache. Grull and the chief stand by the big tent in the middle.
  accept 747                          -- Grull Hawkwind
  accept 752                          -- Chief Hawkwind

step The Hunt Begins
  tip Plainstriders roam the grass all around the camp.
  complete 747

step Grull Hawkwind
  turnin 747
  accept 750
  accept 3091 only Warrior            -- Grull Hawkwind: Simple Note
  accept 3092 only Hunter             -- Grull Hawkwind: Etched Note
  accept 3093 only Shaman             -- Grull Hawkwind: Rune-Inscribed Note
  accept 3094 only Druid              -- Grull Hawkwind: Verdant Note
  turnin 3091 only Warrior            -- Harutt Thunderhorn, the warrior trainer
  turnin 3092 only Hunter             -- Lanka Farshot, the hunter trainer
  turnin 3093 only Shaman             -- Meela Dawnstrider, the shaman trainer in camp
  turnin 3094 only Druid              -- Gart Mistrunner, the druid trainer beside him
  train class

step Greatmother Hawkwind
  tip Greatmother Hawkwind sits by the tent on the camp's eastern edge; the Water Pitcher stands next to her.
  turnin 752
  accept 753
  complete 753

step Chief Hawkwind
  turnin 753
  accept 755

step The Hunt Continues
  tip Antur Fallow stands at the west end of the camp, at the north-west corner of the hills where the Mountain Cougars prowl: take his quest, hunt the cougars from there south and east, then come back up to Grull.
  accept 1656                         -- Antur Fallow
  complete 750

step Grull Hawkwind
  turnin 750
  accept 780
  accept 3376                         -- Brave Windfeather, next to Grull
  train class

step Seer Graytongue
  tip Follow the path south out of camp to the Seer's tent at the foot of the hills.
  turnin 755
  accept 95805
  accept 757

step The shrine of An'she and Mu'sha
  tip The incense burns out in ten minutes: run straight east along the southern hills to the Ritual Fire.
  turnin 95805

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Brambleblade Ravine

step Brambleblade Ravine
  tip Battleboars graze north of the shrine; the Bristleback quilboar hold the ravine to the north-east. Chief Sharptusk Thornmantle stands at its eastern end, and the Dirt-stained Map lies on the ground in the camp.
  complete 780
  complete 757
  complete 3376
  collect 4851
  accept 781

step Camp Narache
  tip Back west to the camp.
  turnin 780                          -- Grull Hawkwind
  turnin 3376                         -- Brave Windfeather
  turnin 781                          -- Chief Hawkwind
  turnin 757
  accept 763
  accept 96659

step Seer Ravenfeather
  only Shaman
  tip Seer Ravenfeather stands in Camp Narache. Call of Earth needs level 4, which you reach with the turn-ins here.
  accept 1519                         -- Seer Ravenfeather

step Ritual Salve
  only Shaman
  tip Back east to Brambleblade Ravine: the Bristleback Shamans stand among the quilboar there.
  collect 6634 quest 1519.1

step Call of Earth
  only Shaman
  tip Back to Seer Ravenfeather in the camp. The Minor Manifestation of Earth waits on the mesa east of the camp: drink the Earth Sapta there to see it, then take the Rough Quartz back to the Seer.
  turnin 1519                         -- Seer Ravenfeather
  accept 1520
  turnin 1520                         -- Minor Manifestation of Earth
  accept 1521
  turnin 1521                         -- Seer Ravenfeather: Stoneskin Totem and your Earth Totem

